{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1475608-aeon-book-page-358-i-ve-always-wondered","id":1475608,"title":"Aeon Book, Page 358. I've always wondered....","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-28T17:08:34-08:00","id":1475608,"title":"Aeon Book, Page 358. I've always wondered....","content":"Hello All:<br /> <br /> So, ever since I bought Trinity back when it was originally called Aeon and came in a snazzy folding plastic cover I have seen the olde photo of the original Aeon Society, with ol' Maxwel Bigbritches in the front looking all stalwart and so forth with his assorted pals and compatriots. And ever since then I have wondered:<br /> <br /> Who were the models/people in that picture?<br /> <br /> Were they employees of White Wolf? Specifically perhaps the production staff of Aeon/Trinity? Were they friends and spouses? Local summer-stock theatrical troupe? Steampunk Cosplay wasn't really that big a deal back then so....local passers by?<br /> <br /> Does anybody know for sure? Just one of those things I've always been curious about....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21614-corradus","name":"Corradus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21614_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-28T18:09:12-08:00","id":1475611,"title":"","content":"I can't say for sure who is who, but I'm fairly certain they were all old WW employees or freelancers. One of the villains in the old Adventure! corebook, The Lone Gunman (pg. 238), looks distnctly like Rob Hatch (look at that scowl and tell me I'm wrong).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25998-loneshark","name":"Loneshark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-28T18:11:26-08:00","id":1475612,"title":"","content":"That's a bunch of the staff, and possibly a couple of freelancers, circa 1996-98.<br /> <br /> - C.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Clayton A. Oliver | Formerly Ubiquitous<br /> <br /> <i>When the half-light starts to rise/And the long gone come back again<br /> After the shortcuts and the highs/Comes the pain<br /> And the rain</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2966-tegyrius","name":"Tegyrius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-28T20:10:34-08:00","id":1475617,"title":"","content":"As I recall, Matt Milberger is Jake &quot;Danger Ace&quot; Stefokowski, Rich Thomas himself is &quot;Safari&quot; Jack Tallon, and Ken Cliffe is Max Mercer. I <i>think</i> that's Justin Achilli as Prof Dixon, although he's portrayed by someone else in other illustrations in Adventure!.<br /> <br /> I don't know who Donighal, Newfield, or Styles are portrayed by. Other staff, freelancers, or friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://f